      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "mkinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-22T07:16:26Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): Fanuc option to write the stock as a Manual Guide i blank\n\nThe stream states the setup's stock as a controller blank: PARAM\nStockBlank (box, cylinder-x/y/z, or why no blank form fits) and\nPARAM StockBlankZBottom. The engine passes both only to a script that\ndeclares stockBlank = true, so every other post (Klartext lists its\nPARAMs and refuses others) posts byte-identical output.\n\nThe Fanuc post has the new boolean option manualGuideBlank (off by\ndefault). With it on, the first section writes G1902 B D H I J K for a\nbox stock, or G1900 D L K for a bar along Z with its axis on the work\norigin, after G21/G20 and before G90. Any other stock, a rotated or\nflipped WCS, or an inverted machine axis writes a comment that says\nwhy, never a block.\n\nFixes #2769\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
